# Paths that follow this checkout into every worktree bin/claude-worktree
# creates. One path per line, relative to the repo root; a line starting with
# `#` is a comment.
# A listed path that does not exist here is skipped, so this list is safe to
# keep even on a checkout that has none of it.
# See dot/claude/rules/worktree-scope.md §6.

# A delegate opens PRs by default, so it needs a GitHub token, and mise reads
# that token via this file. The file is a pointer (`_.file = "~/..."`); the
# secret itself stays under $HOME, so the copy carries nothing sensitive into
# the worktree or the repo.
mise.local.toml
